# exit: 0
# -noproof admits every lemma before the target on its statement alone
# and replays only the proof the position lands inside. Line 32 is the
# second `split.' of `target_and', so the goals here are exactly the
# ones `load-goals'-style plain LOAD reports at that line -- run the
# same LOAD without the flag to see it. The reply tag carries
# [noproof], and `print first_and' shows a skipped lemma is bound and
# usable like any other.
LOAD "fixtures/noproof.ec" 32 -noproof
TREE
print first_and.
